            <ArticleTitle>Kinetically controlled hierarchical self-assemblies of all-trans-retinoic acid on Au(111).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2252-2255</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc08148g</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Kinetically controlled hierarchical self-assemblies of all-trans-retinoic acid on Au(111) were investigated via low-temperature scanning tunneling microscopy in ultra-high vacuum. The dominant molecular hierarchical superstructure could be selectively controlled to dimer, tetramer, or pentamer patterns, which were stabilized by hydrogen bonds and van der Waals interactions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
